# CollaboTicket Typography

CollaboTicket is a Japan-market consulting brand where **text is UI**. The top priority is **readability (읽기 쉬움)**.

## Never do

- Do **not** force line breaks in headings or marketing copy to fit character counts.
- Do **not** use `<br />`, `<br>`, or split strings into arrays for visual line breaks in Hero, section titles, card titles, article titles, or FAQ questions.
- Do **not** create separate mobile/desktop/desktop copy variants for wrapping.

Bad:

```tsx
<h1>
  일본 시장을 분석하
  <br />
  고, 실행까지 합니다.
</h1>
```

## Always do

- Write headings as **one natural Korean sentence** (meaning unit).
- Control wrapping with CSS only: `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `word-break: keep-all`. Prefer natural wrap over early breaks.
- For **article H1**, **insight body h2/h3**, and **FAQ questions**: do **not** use narrow `em` max-width or `text-wrap: pretty` — use `max-width: none`, `text-wrap: wrap`, `line-break: auto` so titles wrap only when the viewport is actually too narrow.
- For hero / section / lead copy, `max-width` (**em** for Korean — not `ch`) and `text-wrap: pretty` are still OK.
- Use shared classes from `lib/typography.ts` and `app/globals.css`:

| Role | Class |
|------|--------|
| Hero H1 | `type-hero` |
| Page hero / hub H1 | `type-display` |
| Section H2 | `type-section-title` |
| Card H3 | `type-card-title` |
| Article H1 | `type-article-title` |
| Sub copy / intro | `type-lead` |
| Body | `type-body` |
| FAQ question | `type-faq-question` |

Helpers: `typeHero()`, `typeSectionTitle()`, etc. in `lib/typography.ts`.

## Centered sections

Add `type-section-title--center` and `type-lead--center` when the block is text-center.

## Insight markdown

Article titles (`type-article-title`) and headings in `.insight-body` wrap naturally. Do not inject `<br>` into markdown titles or FAQ questions.

## Design tone

Minimal (Stripe / Linear / Vercel) layout, but **Korean enterprise-grade readability** — comfortable line length, generous line-height, subtle negative letter-spacing on headings.
